{
  "purpose": "The libc-test programs the libc-test scenario runs (S1.3, S2, S3, S7.1, S7.2, K5.3): those whose needs the substrate has (threads, futex-equivalent waits and signals of the own process, dynamic loading, pipes within a process (R2.3a), but no fork, sockets, writable files or resource limits; at most sixteen threads of a process, K5.3). Every test runs in a process of its own, built statically and dynamically as libc-test builds it; the dynamic-only tests open a shared library of libc-test with dlopen, and the math suite is built dynamically alone, as libc-test builds it. mathExcluded names the math tests left out on an ISA. Every listed run must pass on both ISAs; the reasons for the rest are in S1.3-Libc-Test.md, S2-Threads.md, S7.1-Libc-Test-Processes.md and S7.2-Libc-Test-Math.md.",
